body:
ACCEPT. This closes a demonstrated Scala construction-boundary failure and is finite.

C1-T will enumerate, for every public checked/non-Cartesian type:
1. every declared public/package-visible factory, including unsafe-named paths;
2. apply;
3. copy;
4. companion fromProduct;
5. summon[Mirror.ProductOf[T]].fromProduct.

Each compile-refusal mechanism gets its own same-mechanism positive control so absence of the mechanism cannot make the probe vacuous. Honest Cartesian-product records may explicitly mark a door open; every invariant-bearing relational value must close the door or return through a checked constructor. Each C1 child must instantiate its predeclared matrix rows with the type and laws it lands.

No additional review cycle follows from this amendment. I will include it in the single final superseding C1 sequence after the remaining review returns.
